proof.text:
For the target identity and $f:V\to T$, substitute $\alpha_{\mathrm{id}_T,f}=\lambda_TL_f$ from [prop-functor-package] in Step 2. Naturality of $\lambda_T$ makes the transpose equal to
$$\varepsilon_{\mathrm{id}_T,M}\circ\lambda_{T,R_{\mathrm{id}_T}M}^{-1}\circ\varepsilon_{f,R_{\mathrm{id}_T}M}
=u_{T,M}\circ\varepsilon_{f,R_{\mathrm{id}_T}M}
=\varepsilon_{f,M}\circ L_fR_f(u_{T,M}),$$
where the last equality is counit naturality for $f$. Injectivity gives $\chi_{f,\mathrm{id}_T,M}=R_f(u_{T,M})$. Steps 7 and 8 are therefore the identity comparisons after the canonical identification $R_{\mathrm{id}_T}\cong\mathrm{id}$, even when its specified counit is not literally the identity. Evaluating these identities and the equation of Step 5 at $A_s$ proves functoriality of the isomorphism of Step 3.
